                            key=".1:$<section id=0"Aspects"  class=0"tabbed-narrative">
  <div class=0"section-introduction">
    <div class=0"section-introduction__term">Form</div>
    <div class=0"section-introduction__definition">
      First Act - Shite Performs=2<br>
      <em>Kuri</em> → <em>Sashi</em> → <em><strong>Kuse</strong></em>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class=0"section-introduction">
    <div class=0"section-introduction__term">Synopsis</div>
    <div class=0"section-introduction__definition">
      An account given by the young boy of victorious battles of prince
      Yamato-dake and the power of his sword. Munechika is told to be confident
      about accomplishing his task.
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class=0"section-introduction">
    <div class=0"section-introduction__term">Text</div>
    <div class=0"section-introduction__definition">
      Poetry in
      <a href=0"/text/#Rhythmic-I" target=0"_blank">irregular</a> rhythm.
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class=0"section-introduction">
    <div class=0"section-introduction__term">Music</div>
    <div class=0"section-introduction__definition">
      The text set in
      <a href=0"/music/voices#Hiranori" target=0"_blank"><em>hiranori</em></a> is
      sung in
      <a href=0"/music/voices#Tsuyogin" target=0"_blank"><em>tsuyogin</em></a>
      style by the jiutai with three interventions by the shite. The percussion
      is in
      <a href=0"/music/otsuzumi-kotsuzumi/#strictness" target=0"_blank">strict</a>
      and the nohkan in
      <a href=0"/music/nohkan/#Non-congruent-Strict" target=0"_blank">non-congruent</a>
      rhythmic settings.
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class=0"section-introduction">
    <div class=0"section-introduction__term">Visuals</div>
    <div class=0"section-introduction__definition">
      In the first of three parts, the shite continues to kneel on
      <a href=0"/staging/stage/#Squares" target=0"_blank">Square 9</a> turning
      toward the waki only for the closing line. He then turns back and begins
      the second part ornamented by a sequence of mimetic movements while
      remaining in a kneeling position. The third part consists of an active
      dance involving the full stage. This is the first dance-to-text of the
      play.
    </div>
  </div>
</section>"
