    <div class="section-introduction__definition">n/a</div>
  </div>
  <div class="section-introduction">
    <div class="section-introduction__term">Visuals</div>
    <div class="section-introduction__definition">
      Two stage assistants remove the stage property, before the performers
      leave the stage.
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="intermedia" title="Intermedia" class="tabbed-narrative">
  <p>
    The exit of the actors and musicians happens in silence. The shite is the
    first one to exit, followed by the waki. If a <em>tsukurimono</em> was used
    in the play, the stage assistants would then procede with its removal. In
    all cases, it is once the actor or stage assistant has passed the Second
    pine that the curtain is lifted, and pulled back down once he has entered
    the anteroom. From this point, the musicians exit in the same order they
    entered, nokhan player first, followed by the kotsuzumi, ōtsuzumi,and taiko
    players. Upon reaching the Second pine, the curtain is pulled back partially
    on one side. As for the jiutai members, they exit through the back left side
    door starting with the back row members. Even as they are exiting the stage,
    actors, assistants and musicians exhibit great modesty and decorum. Thus,
    the audience holds its applause until the last musician is about exit.
  </p>
</section>
